---
import GuideLayout from '../../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
const toc=[
  {href:'#overview',label:'Overview'},
  {href:'#access',label:'How to Access'},
  {href:'#obtaining',label:'Obtaining a Pattern'},
  {href:'#applying',label:'Applying a Pattern'},
  {href:'#slots',label:'Slots and Stages'},
  {href:'#upgrading',label:'Upgrading'},
  {href:'#extracting',label:'Extracting a Pattern'},
  {href:'#multidye',label:'Multi Dye'},
  {href:'#priority',label:'Stat Priority'},
  {href:'#mistakes',label:'Common Mistakes'}
];
---
<GuideLayout title="Patterns | L2 Guardian Guides" lang="en" active="patterns" toc={toc}>
<div class="content">
  <a class="back" href="/en/">← Back to home</a>

  <section class="hero"><img src="/images/patterns.png" alt="Pattern system in L2 Reborn Guardian"/><div class="hero-body"><div class="badge">CHARACTER PROGRESSION</div><h1>Patterns</h1><p class="subtitle">Patterns apply permanent base stats and additional bonuses to the character. Progress begins with a selected Stage 0 Dye and continues through upgrades that consume Dye Boosters and Adena.</p><div class="info-grid"><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Available Slots</div><div class="value">3</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Chapter 2 Maximum</div><div class="value">Stage 11</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Daily Materials</div><div class="value">3 Dye Boosters</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Main Priority</div><div class="value">WIT or STR</div></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="section quick-start"><div class="quick-head"><div class="quick-icon">⚡</div><div><h2>Quick Start</h2><p>From daily materials to an active Pattern.</p></div></div><div class="quick-grid"><div class="quick-card"><div class="quick-title">Farm Daily</div><div class="quick-value">3 Dye Boosters</div><span class="quick-tag high">Maximum</span></div><div class="quick-card"><div class="quick-title">Craft Coupon</div><div class="quick-value">5 Boosters + 5m</div><span class="quick-tag high">Guaranteed</span></div><div class="quick-card"><div class="quick-title">Apply Dye</div><div class="quick-value">1.32m Adena</div><span class="quick-tag high">Stage 0</span></div><div class="quick-card"><div class="quick-title">Upgrade Attempt</div><div class="quick-value">1 Booster</div><span class="quick-tag medium">10k Adena</span></div></div><div class="quick-footer"><div class="quick-tip"><strong>Choose the correct stat</strong>Most magical characters should prioritize WIT first, while physical characters should prioritize STR.</div><div class="quick-tip"><strong>Failures build pity</strong>Failed attempts keep the current Stage and add progress toward a guaranteed upgrade.</div><div class="quick-tip"><strong>Stage 11 is a long goal</strong>Higher Stages require patience, Adena and many daily Dye Boosters.</div></div></section>

  <section class="section" id="overview"><h2>Overview</h2><p>Each Pattern is based on one of the six base stats: STR, INT, DEX, WIT, CON or MEN. The chosen Dye determines the main stat increased by the Pattern and the additional bonuses unlocked as its Stage rises.</p><p>Patterns are always active after being applied. Three slots are currently available and the same stat can be used in several slots. A fourth slot belongs to future content and is not currently unlocked.</p><div class="note"><strong>Chapter progression:</strong> additional Pattern Stages will become available through later chapters. During Chapter 2, the maximum available Stage is 11.</div></section>

  <section class="section" id="access"><h2>How to Access Patterns</h2><div class="steps"><div class="step"><div class="num">1</div><div><strong>Open the main menu</strong><p>Click the menu button in the bottom right corner of the game interface.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">2</div><div><strong>Select Pattern</strong><p>Click the Pattern icon to view the active slots, apply or delete a Pattern and access Pattern upgrade.</p></div></div></div><figure class="guide-figure wide"><img src="/images/patterns-menu.png" alt="Pattern icon in the main game menu"/><figcaption>The Pattern window is opened from the general menu in the bottom right corner.</figcaption></figure></section>

  <section class="section" id="obtaining"><h2>Obtaining a Stage 0 Pattern</h2><p>A maximum of <strong>3 Dye Boosters per day</strong> can be obtained by defeating normal open world monsters. Monsters with a green title do not provide these daily Dye Boosters.</p><div class="steps"><div class="step"><div class="num">1</div><div><strong>Collect 5 Dye Boosters</strong><p>The daily limit means that obtaining enough materials for a coupon takes at least two days.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">2</div><div><strong>Open Special Craft</strong><p>Go to Upgrade / Growth, select Upgrade and choose Sealed Dye Coupon.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">3</div><div><strong>Craft the coupon</strong><p>The guaranteed craft costs 5 Dye Boosters and 5,000,000 Adena.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">4</div><div><strong>Select a Dye</strong><p>Right click the Sealed Dye Coupon and exchange it for one Stage 0 STR, CON, DEX, INT, MEN or WIT Pattern Dye.</p></div></div></div><div class="guide-gallery"><figure><img src="/images/patterns-coupon-craft.png" alt="Sealed Dye Coupon in Special Craft"/><figcaption>Special Craft path and the complete coupon cost.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/images/patterns-dye-selection.png" alt="Stage 0 Pattern Dye selection window"/><figcaption>The coupon lets the player choose any of the six Stage 0 Dyes.</figcaption></figure></div></section>

  <section class="section" id="applying"><h2>Applying a Pattern</h2><p>Open the Pattern window and click <strong>Apply pattern</strong> under an empty slot. Select the Dye, review the base stat change and confirm the application.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Cost or Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pattern Dye</td><td>1 selected Stage 0 Dye</td></tr><tr><td>Application fee</td><td class="bad">1,320,000 Adena</td></tr><tr><td>Initial bonus</td><td class="good">+1 to the selected base stat</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="guide-gallery effects"><figure><img src="/images/patterns-apply-slot.png" alt="Empty Pattern slots with Apply pattern button"/><figcaption>Select any of the three available slots.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/images/patterns-apply-selection.png" alt="Pattern Dye selection before applying"/><figcaption>Only Dyes currently held in the inventory can be selected.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/images/patterns-apply-confirmation.png" alt="STR Pattern application confirmation and Adena cost"/><figcaption>Review the stat change and the 1.32 million Adena fee before confirming.</figcaption></figure></div></section>

  <section class="section" id="slots"><h2>Slots and Pattern Stages</h2><p>The three available slots can be combined freely. Several Patterns of the same stat may be applied at the same time, so a character can focus multiple slots on WIT or STR while working toward an important base stat breakpoint. Magical characters can transition toward INT Patterns after securing the recommended WIT thresholds.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Example STR Stage</th><th>Visible Bonuses</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Stage 0</td><td>STR +1</td></tr><tr><td>Stage 1</td><td>STR +2</td></tr><tr><td>Stage 2</td><td>STR +3</td></tr><tr><td>Stage 3</td><td>STR +4 and P. Atk. +15</td></tr><tr><td>Stage 4</td><td>STR +4 and P. Atk. +30</td></tr><tr><td>Stage 11</td><td>STR +5 and P. Atk. +130</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><strong>Important progression point:</strong> the selected base stat reaches +4 at Stage 3 but does not reach +5 until Stage 11. The intermediate Stages continue improving additional bonuses associated with that Dye.</div></section>

  <section class="section" id="upgrading"><h2>Upgrading a Pattern</h2><p>Click <strong>Pattern upgrade</strong>, select one of the applied Patterns and attempt Enhancement. Every attempt consumes 1 Dye Booster and 10,000 Adena. Failure leaves the Pattern at its current Stage.</p><figure class="guide-figure wide"><img src="/images/patterns-upgrade-entry.png" alt="Pattern upgrade button below the active slots"/><figcaption>Pattern upgrade is available from the bottom of the main Pattern window.</figcaption></figure><figure class="guide-figure compact"><img src="/images/patterns-upgrade-window.png" alt="Pattern upgrade window showing rate, Dye Booster and Adena cost"/><figcaption>Select an applied Pattern to see its current success rate and exact attempt cost.</figcaption></figure><table><thead><tr><th>Upgrade</th><th>Success Rate</th><th>Dye Booster</th><th>Adena</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Stage 0 to 1</td><td class="good">50%</td><td>1</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><td>Stage 1 to 2</td><td>25%</td><td>1</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><td>Stage 2 to 3</td><td>20%</td><td>1</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><td>Stage 3 to 4</td><td>15%</td><td>1</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><td>Stage 4 to 5</td><td>10%</td><td>1</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><td>Stage 5 to 6</td><td>8%</td><td>1</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><td>Stage 6 to 7</td><td>6%</td><td>1</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><td>Stage 7 to 8</td><td>5%</td><td>1</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><td>Stage 8 to 9</td><td>5%</td><td>1</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><td>Stage 9 to 10</td><td>5%</td><td>1</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><td>Stage 10 to 11</td><td>5%</td><td>1</td><td>10,000</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><strong>Autoupgrade:</strong> this button automates repeated upgrade attempts. It does not change the Pattern progression rules shown above.</div></section>

  <section class="section" id="extracting"><h2>Extracting or Replacing a Pattern</h2><p>To remove a Pattern, click <strong>Delete pattern</strong> beneath the desired slot. The extraction confirmation displays the base stat change before the Pattern is removed.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Extraction</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Fixed fee</td><td class="bad">13,200,000 Adena</td></tr><tr><td>Recovered item</td><td class="good">The Pattern Dye at its current Stage</td></tr><tr><td>Slot</td><td>Becomes available for another Pattern</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="guide-gallery"><figure><img src="/images/patterns-delete-slot.png" alt="Delete pattern button under an INT Pattern"/><figcaption>Choose the exact slot that should be cleared.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/images/patterns-extraction.png" alt="Pattern extraction confirmation with fixed Adena cost"/><figcaption>Extraction costs 13.2 million Adena and returns the Dye without lowering its Stage.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="warning"><strong>Plan before applying:</strong> extraction preserves the Dye, but the fixed 13.2 million Adena fee makes frequent Pattern changes expensive.</div></section>

  <section class="section" id="multidye"><h2>Multi Dye System</h2><p>Each slot can hold two different Patterns through the Multi Dye system. The player can switch freely between them while outside combat, allowing different Pattern sets for different content.</p><figure class="guide-figure wide"><img src="/images/multidye.jpg" alt="Multi Dye Pattern selection system"/><figcaption>Multi Dye provides an alternative Pattern for each slot and allows switching outside combat.</figcaption></figure><div class="note"><strong>Common use:</strong> maintain one Pattern configuration for PvE and another for Olympiad or PvP events.</div></section>

  <section class="section" id="priority"><h2>Stat Priority</h2><div class="steps"><div class="step"><div class="num">1</div><div><strong>Magical characters prioritize WIT first</strong><p>Use WIT Patterns to reach 50 WIT and consider around 60 WIT while Magic Skill Critical Rate remains more valuable than the 60 or 70 INT breakpoints. After securing enough critical frequency, work toward 90 INT.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">2</div><div><strong>Physical characters prioritize STR</strong><p>Use STR Patterns while working toward a total of 90 STR, then progress toward 60 DEX.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">3</div><div><strong>Check every relevant breakpoint</strong><p>Read <a href="/en/guides/character/#stats">Base Stats and Breakpoints</a> in the Character guide before distributing Pattern slots. Your Pattern setup should support the next useful threshold instead of following one fixed stat forever.</p></div></div></div><div class="note"><strong>Multiple matching Patterns are valid:</strong> because the same stat can be applied in several slots, use matching Patterns when they help reach the next recommended breakpoint.</div></section>

  <section class="section" id="mistakes"><h2>Common Mistakes</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>Why It Matters</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Choosing a Dye before checking character breakpoints</td><td>The Pattern may not help reach the character's next important stat bonus.</td></tr><tr><td>Expecting Stage 11 quickly</td><td class="bad">Daily Dye Booster limits and low success rates make it a slow, expensive goal.</td></tr><tr><td>Forgetting the Pattern application fee</td><td class="bad">Applying a Dye to a Pattern slot costs 1.32 million Adena.</td></tr><tr><td>Ignoring the extraction fee</td><td class="bad">Replacing an applied Pattern always costs 13.2 million Adena.</td></tr><tr><td>Using green title monsters for daily Boosters</td><td>Only normal open world monsters count toward this material source.</td></tr><tr><td>Forgetting that pity is individual</td><td>Progress accumulated on one Pattern does not transfer to another.</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="warning"><strong>Keep realistic expectations:</strong> improving a Pattern to Stage 11 is intentionally expensive and slow. Consistent daily progress is more useful than becoming frustrated by individual failed attempts.</div></section>
</div>
</GuideLayout>
